      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew when the Louis Southwestern Railroad laid tracks, allowing timber and other resources to be shipped out of the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piggott%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Both the home and barn studio of the Hemingway‑Pfeiffer family are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piggott%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Scenes from the 1956 film \"A Face in the Crowd\" starring Andy Griffith were shot on Piggott streets, and photos hang in the local museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.piggottchamberofcommerce.com/planyourvisit",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Piggott sits on Crowley’s Ridge, a natural loess formation that rises from flatlands, giving the town a small‑mount feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piggott%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Piggott is one of two county seats of Clay County, sharing the role with Corning.",
